  "concept": {
    "movement": "A long balanced lateral four-beat walk, with visible upper-leg motion and a quiet back. Faster travel becomes a brisk grounded pace, with gentle neck following and a centered hanging tail.",
    "attack": "A deliberate neck-and-head sweep loads to the right, then cuts fully across to the left from a braced stance. The body supports the neck arc before the head and forefeet recover together.",
    "death": "The knees fold under the tall body before it rolls onto a supported flank. The long articulated neck and skull settle with the torso; released hooves relax into a still hold, and the tail follows the rump coherently."
